b/ref 17592186341908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068700 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068700 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068700 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068700 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1045 "Left and Right Continuity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068998 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "acac3ae8-22e4-541d-b0da-b38b7e642d06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1061 12117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "27206838-7dfd-50f0-a4b5-a92905b05017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069571 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1061 12118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b43b6d85-ec3f-5921-878b-59ca9e5c066f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069572 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 #edb/ref 1061 12119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55c60e5f-cbe7-5688-8af0-b8fa5d2c54d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069573 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069574 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069574 #edb/ref 1061 12120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069574 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b88e81b2-e4ca-5ffc-8ade-1a44b0fecea1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069574 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069575 #edb/ref 1061 12121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069575 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1017d5f3-a1be-5979-aa84-1860d0b66f77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069575 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069577 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069577 #edb/ref 1061 12456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069577 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c70c04f3-5555-555a-93b3-8518806961e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069577 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069959 #edb/ref 1064 "A function $f(x)$ is said to be **left-continuous** at the point $x=c$ if the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x\\to c^-} f(x) = f(c).\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the function $y=f(x)$ defined on the interval $(-\\infty,2]$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/14/14b92b0e5a0f482b5e58da975f6f8d369890af97ddc562a4876e41c496f5dfef.png)\n\nNotice that at $x=2,$ the left limit exists, while right limit does not exist because $f(x)$ is not defined for $x>2.$\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 2^-}f(x) = 4, \\qquad \\lim_{x\\to 2^+}f(x) = \\text{DNE}\n$$\n\nBecause the right-sided limit does not exist, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 2}f(x) = \\text{DNE}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=2.$ However, because the left-sided limit exists and is equal to the function value at $x=2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 2^-}f(x) = 4 = f(2),\n$$\n\nwe can say that the function is **left-continuous** at $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069959 #edb/ref 1065 2596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069959 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "75d31b95-b022-5133-8b0d-54a5ba38c74f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069959 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069960 #edb/ref 1064 "A function $f(x)$ is said to be **right-continuous** at the point $x=c$ if the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x\\to c^+} f(x) = f(c).\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the function $y=f(x)$ defined on the interval $[-2,\\infty)$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/0b/0b625f271c8889466c2a19ed8a333b05e70c2e852058cc1d4469f428d761c799.png)\n\nThe function is **right-continuous** at $x=-2$ because\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to -2^+}f(x) = 4 = f(-2).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069960 #edb/ref 1065 2597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069960 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9424b0a9-43f3-5c35-b8b9-b78b9c69e816" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069960 #edb/ref 1067 "Right Continuity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069962 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that a function $f(x)$ is said to be **continuous** at a point $x=c$ if \n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to c} f(x) = f(c) .\n$$\n\nIn order for the above statement to be true, we require both\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {c}^{-}}f(x)=f(c)\\,\\text{and}\\,{lim}_{x\\to {c}^{+}}f(x)=f(c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equalities represent left-continuity and right-continuity. So, we have the following fact:\n\n> A function is **continuous** at a point if and only if it is *both* **left-continuous** *and* **right-continuous** at that point." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069962 #edb/ref 1065 2641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069962 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1dd8ea3c-49f9-5c85-98b3-85b0542e7a8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069962 #edb/ref 1067 "Defining Continuity in Terms of Left-Continuity and Right-Continuity" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324420 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324420 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "374ae646-8b4e-5b0e-bd7e-4acb5d1c0ed8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325026 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325026 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325026 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7d1612fc-e261-50ce-9313-fe26f50738e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325709 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325709 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325709 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c86a33ca-8732-5643-a35e-d2538c0e58e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325813 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325813 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325813 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d3e6cb1a-5418-5746-8b18-030e1c8789a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326089 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326089 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326089 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0206e22-2c8b-5150-92b8-e52b0d52a598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186326089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186324420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326375 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5b0c2133-1c76-5099-a8ab-82d13698a8d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8f/8fdb835ed2998fae4d8afc3fd5e593bac6c72b1ee45c8b4fe01bdc4348322d1e.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\n\nII. The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\n\nIII. The function is continuous at $x=-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa66e43c-92cc-5831-9942-3be250ef9ed8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326691 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339588 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339588 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339588 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33ab5c9a-741e-507f-8a99-07a9f7aa451c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339663 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339663 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339663 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bf55990-23dc-5